From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] portal-access-manager: Allow Once, Always Allow and Don't
 Allow

Plinius: every access question of the phone has the same three buttons,
one below the other: "Allow Once", "Always Allow" and "Don't Allow"
(AppAuthPrompt:buttons). The access dialog asks every portal request
that way; plinius-appaccess's questions about USB cameras, security keys
and the network come through the same dialog.

xdg-desktop-portal 1.22.1 (read in its source: camera.c, location.c,
screenshot.c, wallpaper.c, background.c) knows granted (0) and denied
(1) only and keeps the answer in the permission store for good:

- camera: table "devices", id "camera", "yes"/"no", written only when
  the app had no entry (measured on the phone: Snapshot, Fractal and
  Emilia with ['yes'])
- location: table "location", id "location", [accuracy, last use],
  e.g. ['EXACT', '<timestamp>'] (measured for Fractal); asked only
  without an entry, written after every dialog, "NONE" for a denial
- screenshot, wallpaper: tables and ids of that name, "yes"/"no", only
  without an entry
- background: asked only while the entry says "ask", nothing written

"Always Allow" answers granted, "Don't Allow" denied; both are stored
as before. "Allow Once", and a dialog swiped away, answer granted or
denied, but the entry xdg-desktop-portal writes for them is deleted
again (access-once.c): before the answer the app's entries of the four
tables above are looked up, then the first Changed signal of the
permission store (emitted for every table on every change, read in
document-portal/xdg-permission-store.c) within 10 s that gives the app
an entry it had not is undone with DeletePermission. Limits: another
new entry of the same app in one of these tables within these 10 s is
deleted instead; a write later than that stays.

A caller that handles "Allow Once" itself passes "plinius-once" (b),
its entries are left alone; "plinius-buttons" (as of "once", "always",
"never") names the buttons to show. Every answer has "plinius-choice"
(s: "once", "always", "never" or "cancel"). The icon may also be a
file, as desktop files name icons.
